Backport of grpc-go commit ecbf7d6d (grpc/grpc-go#9533, released in v1.85.0)
to the grpc-go v1.83.2 that containerd 2.4.2 requires.

transport: prevent nil pointer dereference in recvBuffer.put.

A client that sends a second DATA frame with END_STREAM on a stream whose
unary handler has already returned makes recvBuffer.put free the nil buffer
of an io.EOF message, and the whole containerd process panics in
http2Server.handleData (podster-uqb.138, conformance run 15).

--- a/internal/transport/transport.go
+++ b/internal/transport/transport.go
@@ -121,7 +121,9 @@ func (b *recvBuffer) put(r recvMsg) {
 	if b.err != nil {
 		// drop the buffer on the floor. Since b.err is not nil, any subsequent reads
 		// will always return an error, making this buffer inaccessible.
-		r.buffer.Free()
+		if r.buffer != nil {
+			r.buffer.Free()
+		}
 		// An error had occurred earlier, don't accept more
 		// data or errors.
 		return
